  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1258 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures across the area are in the low 70s with \nwinds out of the north. The HRRR smoke model is again showing some \nnear surface smoke but the only effect should be a slight smoke \nsmell to the air. Up aloft, there looks to be some smoke as well, \nlending a slight haziness to the sky. Highs today will be about 10 \ndegrees cooler and then slowly increase through the rest of the work \nweek. \n\nOur next chance for precipitation looks to be concentrated over \nsouth central SD tonight into Wednesday morning. This is expected to \nstay showers. Another round comes through Thursday afternoon and \nevening. This may bring a chance of thunderstorms to areas west of \nthe James River, although it is hard to say if any storms will \nbecome severe at this time. Heat returns Friday into the weekend. \nModels ran high on temperatures in areas with higher humidity during \nthe last heat wave so we will see if similar high bias shows up for \nthis weekend. This round looks to be less humid, so models may \nhandle it better. Current forecast has highs in the 90s to low 100s, \nhighest over central SD. Temperatures going into next work week look \nto start a cooling trend.",
